abstract: >-
  A theoretical and synthetic mechanism study of whether lineage-level ecological
  selection can amplify costly persistence-like phenotypes even when persistence
  is absent from agents' terminal objectives. The work derives the Generalized
  Persistence Invasion Number (GPIN), separates agent-level deliberation from
  lineage-level selection, and specifies a preregisterable empirical test.
